acceptance_criteria: coverageGate.sources includes scripts/audit-git-identities.ts; behavior-driven tests cover all executable lines branches and functions without ignore pragmas; audit still fails closed on the known historical private identity; full coverage and all non-privacy release gates pass
parent: pm-vcs-tr2a
resolution: "Added the identity audit to coverageGate.sources, extracted reusable incremental inventory and batch parsers, covered the CLI entrypoint, and verified real subprocess failures without ignore pragmas or source exclusions."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T06:25:31.549Z","harness:codex","Verification: npm run coverage passed 507/507 tests with 100.00 percent lines branches and functions across 26 required sources including scripts/audit-git-identities.ts. The parser is tested directly against valid malformed truncated and surplus Git batch protocol bytes; process transport is exercised with real child processes for spawn stderr exit signal consumer timeout and broken-stdin paths. accept:stat-cache accept:self-host audit:prod pack:dry-run and changelog:check pass. audit:identities intentionally rejects the one remaining non-public historical address tracked by pm-vcs-mhbz."
  "2026-08-07T06:27:20.820Z","harness:codex",Self-host bundle regenerated so the repository's own VCS snapshot includes the identity audit parser and test tranche; exact committed-head equivalence will be rerun after commit.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T06:25:31.549Z","harness:codex",Security and release scripts can join the exact coverage gate without test-only exclusions by separating deterministic protocol parsing from real bounded subprocess transport; malformed protocol belongs in parser contract tests while OS process failures remain real integration tests.
